    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d683">

                <pb facs="0714" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.24/132a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-22T20:00:00-05:00">March 22, 1941—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>108. On March 17 the Department issued licenses for the export to Greece of the
                    following arms and ammunition released under the provisions of the Act of March
                    11, 1941:<anchor n="93" xml:id="d683-f1"/> Fifty 75-millimeter guns, 150,000 <pb
                        facs="0715" n="703" xml:id="pg703"/> shells for these guns, and 30,000
                    shells for 155-millimeter howitzers.<anchor n="94" xml:id="d683-f2"/> The
                    appropriate authorities of this Government are now considering carefully what
                    further arms and other materials can be released for export to Greece under the
                    authority of this law. You may so inform the Greek Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d683-f1" n="93" xml:id="d683-f1-content">
                <p>Lend-Lease Act; 55 Stat. 31.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d683-f2" n="94" xml:id="d683-f2-content">
                <p>The foregoing material was from ordnance stock transferred by the War Department
                    to the Greek Government by direction of the President.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
